+---
+tags: [decision, operations, security]
+---
+
+# Admin-only endpoint for recent operations
+
+## Decision
+
+`GET /api/operations/recent` returns the operations whose `date` lies between now minus 30 days and now, inclusive.
+It is restricted to the `ADMIN` authority in two places: a URL matcher in `SecurityConfiguration` and `@PreAuthorize` on the resource method.
+The response is paged with `Pageable` and pagination headers, and the sort parameter is checked against an allow-list (`id`, `date`, `description`, `amount`).
+
+## Why
+
+- The user asked for this exact path, so it sits under `/api/operations` rather than `/api/admin`, which `docs/api.md` would otherwise suggest for admin views.
+- A 30-day window can still grow large, so the endpoint pages instead of returning an unbounded list, as `docs/backend.md` requires.
+- The window is a business rule, so it lives in `OperationService` and reads the current time from an injected `Clock`.
+- Operations dated after now are excluded, which follows the literal reading of "within the last 30 days".
+
+## Consequences
+
+- A `Clock` bean was added in `config/ClockConfiguration` (system UTC); no other code had one.
+- Labels are fetched with the same bag-relationship query the list endpoint uses.
+
+Related: [[2026-11-01]], [[index]].
